// Code signing.
//
// "-" is ad-hoc signing: it needs no setup and builds anywhere, which is why it
// is the default here. The cost is that an ad-hoc signature is a hash of the
// binary's contents, so it changes on every build — and macOS identifies apps to
// TCC (Accessibility, Input Monitoring, Microphone) by that hash. Every rebuild
// therefore looks like a brand new app, and the permissions you granted are
// attached to a build that no longer exists. The toggles stay lit in System
// Settings while the running app is denied.
//
// Signing with a certificate instead swaps that hash for the certificate's, which
// never changes. Grant the permissions once and they hold across every rebuild.
//
// To switch, create a local certificate and point at it from an untracked file —
// see "Making permissions stick" in the README. Nothing personal is committed.

CODE_SIGN_IDENTITY = -

// Optional and untracked. If it doesn't exist this line does nothing.
#include? "Signing.local.xcconfig"
